{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.und.edu/jobs/teaching-assistant-professor-grand-forks-north-dakota-united-states-ebb1380d-d156-4a3c-8fb3-8f59012d008e": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Teaching Assistant Professor - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Teaching Assistant Professor - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Kiosk mode Teaching Assistant Professor Apply Now Teaching Assistant Professor 499755 Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Full-time Faculty Salary/Position Classification $26,000 4.5 month contract, Exempt 40 hours per week This position will work onsite at UND Grand Forks, ND campus Purpose of Position The Department of Mathematics & Statistics at the University of North Dakota is seeking a teaching assistant professor. This 4.5-month, non-tenure-track position is contingent on availability of funding. The Mathematics & Statistics Department is housed in the College of Arts & Sciences and currently offers a BS in Mathematics, MS and MEd in Mathematics, and MS in Applied Statistics. The department, one of the largest at UND, consists of 28 faculty and teaches thousands of students each year at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The Department of Mathematics & Statistics at the University of North Dakota is seeking a Teaching Assistant Professor. This is a 4.5-month, non-tenure-track position that will serve students in a variety of 100- and 200-level courses in both on-campus and online modalities. Position is open for renewal for the following academic year based on job performance, instructional demand, and available budget. Established in 1883, the University of North Dakota is the oldest research university in North Dakota. Founded with a strong liberal arts foundation, it is the state’s flagship university and is classified by the Carnegie Foundation as having very high research activity. UND offers degrees in more than 225 fields of study with nearly 16,000 students. It is the home of the state’s only School of Law and School of Medicine. The School of Medicine and Health Sciences has major initiatives in rural and public health, and Aerospace is home to one of the first and largest unmanned aerial vehicle programs in the world. UND is located in Grand Forks, North Dakota, a vibrant college town of roughly 60,000 people located on the border of North Dakota and Minnesota. Short commutes, a great public-school system, high-quality medical facilities, low crime, ample parks and theaters, and a cost of living below that found in large American cities are some of Grand Forks’ advantages. Ranked as one of the top 5 Best Small College Towns, and America’s Best Hockey Town, Grand Forks offers stellar quality of life without the metropolitan hassles. Duties & Responsibilities The successful applicant will receive a contract with an approximate distribution of 95% teaching and 5% service effort. UND and the College of Arts & Sciences value a broad range of perspectives and seek applicants who are committed to helping students from underrepresented backgrounds succeed. The University of North Dakota is supportive of dual-career assistance both within the University and the local community. Please contact UND’s Recruiting Manager, Hannah Whalen ( Hannah.Whalen@UND.edu ), to explore dual-career opportunities. Teach 100- and 200-level undergraduate courses in mathematics, including both on-campus (in-person) courses and term-based online courses. Work collaboratively with other Mathematics & Statistics Department faculty to achieve consistent and high-quality learning environments. Required Competencies Excellent written and oral communication skills The ability to teach and inspire students Effective interpersonal skills, including the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, and students Ability to work with and engage students and colleagues with a broad range of backgrounds within and outside the Department of Mathematics & Statistics Competent in using technology and the ability to adopt new tools for both on-campus and online course delivery. Minimum Requirements Earned M.S. in Mathematics by December 31, 2026. Successful completion of a Criminal History Background Check In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the US and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. This position does not support visa sponsorship for continued employment. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience in mathematics in courses commonly taken by first-year college students Familiarity with adaptive learning platforms for facilitating student work in mathematics courses Experience working in a collaborative teaching environment with coordinated course and curricular elements To Apply To assure full consideration, applications must be received by October 29, 2026 and include the following materials: Cover letter CV A statement outlining teaching experience, specifically addressing the applicant’s experience relative to the position’s minimum and preferred qualifications. Names and contact information (email and phone number) for three professional references who are able to address the applicant’s qualifications for this position. Unofficial transcripts. Please note that the selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts upon hire. Position is open until filled. Questions can be directed to the Department Chair, Ryan Zerr, at ryan.zerr@und.edu. Please note, all employment postings close at 11:55pm CST. Position Benefits Benefits include single or family health care coverage (UND pays the full premium), life insurance, employee assistance program, retirement plans with generous employer contributions, sick leave in addition to paid holidays. Optional benefits include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, supplemental retirement plans. UND also offers an employee tuition waiver and a variety of professional development opportunities . Find out more about UND's great benefits and perks ! Categories: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Department: Mathematics Other UND Career Openings There are currently no jobs matching this criteria Apply Now First Name (required) 8986d2e2 Last Name (required) 6ea05cff Email (required) 13e58916 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you Additional Information Find out why Grand Forks is Cooler . All information listed in this position announcement will be used by Human Resources, the Hiring Department, and Civil Rights & Title IX for screening, interviewing and selection purposes. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at UND.humanresources@UND.edu or contact us by phone at 701-777-4226. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Veteran’s Preference Veterans claiming preference must submit all proof of eligibility by the closing date. Proof of eligibility includes a DD-214 or a copy of NGB 22 from National Guard or Reserve (with a unit located in ND) or certification from the applicant's unit command that the individual is expected to be discharged or released from active duty in the uniformed services under other than dishonorable conditions not later than one hundred twenty days after the date of the submission of the certification. If claiming disabled veteran status, proof of eligibility includes a DD-214 and a current letter of disability dated within the past year. Confidentiality of Application Materials Pursuant to NDCC 44-04-18.27, applications and any records related to the applications that identify an applicant are confidential, except records related to the finalists of the position, which are open to the public after the search committee has identified the top three or more finalists who will be invited to campus. EEO Statement The University of North Dakota is an equal opportunity employer (veteran/disability). All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin (including shared ancestry/ethnicity), religion, sex, age, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran's status, or other protected characteristic. Veterans and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Campus Crime Statistics Act, the University of North Dakota publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at UND.edu. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the UND Police Department located at 3851 Campus Road, Grand Forks, ND, 58202. Close Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.und.edu/jobs/professor-of-practice-in-educational-leadership-grand-forks-north-dakota-united-states": {
      "title": "Professor of Practice in Educational Leadership",
      "description": "Professor of Practice in Educational Leadership - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Professor of Practice in Educational Leadership - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Kiosk mode Professor of Practice in Educational Leadership Apply Now Professor of Practice in Educational Leadership 499695 Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Full-time Faculty Salary/Position Classification $37,500 Annual, Exempt, Fully Benefited 20 hours per week This position will work onsite at UND Grand Forks, ND campus Purpose of Position The Department of Teaching, Leadership, and Professional Practice (TLPP) invites applications for a part-time (50% FTE) Professor of Practice in Educational Leadership, with a focus on rural teaching and leadership. This position is housed in the Educational Leadership program in the College of Education and Human Development. Greater Grand Forks area is preferred as work location; however, remote work will be considered, with some required in-person expectations for cohort milestone activities on the UND campus and some travel to North Dakota school sites of cohort participants. This is a two-year special appointment beginning January 2027 and concluding at the end of Fall semester 2028, contingent on available grant funding. The purpose of this position is to support the Rural Master of Science in Teaching & Leadership (MSTL) Tuition Scholarship Cohort, made possible by a grant from the Burgum Foundation, a cohort of approximately 30 rural North Dakota educators earning the MSTL degree from Spring 2027 through Fall 2028. The Professor of Practice is the primary instructional, coaching, and field-connection role for this cohort, serving as the bridge between UND’s Educational Leadership programs and the rural districts, schools, and classrooms where cohort members live, teach, and lead. Duties & Responsibilities Teaching Teach up to two graduate courses per semester for the Burgum rural cohort and the Educational Leadership program over the term of appointment, in online asynchronous and synchronous formats. Adapt course delivery, pacing, and assessment to the realities of full-time rural practitioners, including multi-role educators, multi- grade classrooms, resource-constrained settings, and geographically dispersed participants. Design and facilitate synchronous cohort sessions that build a durable statewide network among rural cohort members. Maintain skills in rural school and district leadership practice and integrate those skills into instruction. Coaching and Advising Serve as the coach of record for all Burgum cohort participants across the full program, from cohort launch through degree completion. Conduct regular individual coaching conversations with each participant, including on-site visits to participant districts where feasible. Provide academic advising, including program-of-study planning, specialization guidance, and progression monitoring. Monitor participant progress and retention proactively; identify participants at risk of stopping out and coordinate timely support. Support participants in identifying, pursuing, and securing teacher leadership, school-based, or district-based leadership roles in North Dakota. Rural Professional Projects Guide each participant in identifying an authentic, high-value professional project rooted in a real challenge or opportunity in the participant’s home district. Mentor participants through project design to presentation, ensuring both practical field value and appropriate scholarly rigor for the MSTL professional project requirement. Broker connections between participants and district leaders, regional education associations, exemplary rural programs, and state-level partners in support of project work. District Partnership and Program Service Cultivate and sustain relationships with participating rural North Dakota districts, superintendents, principals, and regional education associations to create field learning opportunities and support participant success. Collaborate with district leaders to align cohort learning experiences with district needs and participant career aspirations. Provide participation, progress, and retention information on the cohort as requested. Support cohort recruitment, admissions review, onboarding, and milestone events, including graduation. Participate in Educational Leadership program, department, college, and university service appropriate to a Professor of Practice appointment, and in relevant professional associations. Represent UND and the MSTL program at North Dakota education conferences, regional meetings, and district events. Successful applicants should have teaching, coaching, and service interests that align with the Educational Leadership or Educational Administration field and demonstrated effectiveness as an educational leadership practitioner in North Dakota with expertise in school and/or district leadership, school-community partnerships, instructional leadership, and the development of teacher and school leaders. Applicants must also have a commitment to addressing diversity, inclusion, and equity in education. UND and the College of Education and Human Development value a broad range of perspectives and seek applicants who are committed to helping students from all backgrounds succeed. Required Competencies Excellent written and verbal communication skills The ability to teach, inspire, and mentor graduate students Effective interpersonal skills, including the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and K-12 partners Competent in using technology and ability to adopt new tools for course delivery and coaching students Willingness and ability to be present on the UND campus for cohort milestone events, and to travel to campus for those events and to participant districts as feasible, consistent with a part-time appointment and the appointee’s location in North Dakota Minimum Requirements Master’s degree in Educational Leadership or Educational Administration At least ten years of documented professional experience in a North Dakota school leadership and/or district leadership role Demonstrated experience coaching and mentoring practicing educators Successful completion of criminal history records check In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the US and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. This position does not support visa sponsorship for continued employment. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctorate (EdD or PhD) in Educational Leadership or Educational Administration Service as a principal, superintendent, assistant superintendent, or central office leader in a rural and/or small North Dakota school district Experience teaching graduate education courses and/or online courses Established relationships across North Dakota’s rural education landscape, including districts, regional education associations, the ND Department of Public Instruction, and state professional associations To Apply To assure full consideration, applications must be received by 11/09/2026 and include the following materials: Cover letter addressing each required and preferred qualification, with specific evidence of effectiveness in a North Dakota school leadership and/or district leadership role Curriculum Vitae or Resume A brief statement (no more than two pages) describing the applicant’s approach to coaching and developing practicing educators Three professional references with complete contact information The position will remain open until filled. Please note, all employment postings close at 11:55pm CST. Position Benefits Benefits include single or family health care coverage (UND pays the full premium), life insurance, employee assistance program, retirement plans with generous employer contributions, sick leave in addition to paid holidays. Optional benefits include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, supplemental retirement plans. UND also offers an employee tuition waiver and a variety of professional development opportunities . Find out more about UND's great benefits and perks ! Want to be notified of similar opportunities? First Name (required) 7b1ce4fe Last Name (required) b6913057 Email (required) ea09d32f Job Alert bdae2ddb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Teaching & Leadership Teaching & Leadership Categories Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you for your interest in applying to the University of North Dakota Categories: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Department: Teaching & Leadership Other UND Career Openings Associate Dean for Research and Innovation Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Education & Human Development The College of Education & Human Development invites applications to lead our college as the Associate Dean for Research and Innovation. Assistant Professor of Forensic Science, Tenure Track Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Criminal Justice The Forensic Science Program in the College of Arts & Sciences at the University of North Dakota invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Forensic Science. Associate Vice President for Research and Innovation/Chief Operating Officer Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States VP Research & Economic Dev The University of North Dakota is seeking candidates for the position of Associate Vice President for Research and Innovation / Chief Operating Officer (AVPRI/COO). UND is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission (HLC) and is classified Carnegie R1 (Very High Research Activity) with annual research expenditures approaching $200 million. Apply Now First Name (required) 8a4433ec Last Name (required) da513d43 Email (required) 839f7276 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you Additional Information Find out why Grand Forks is Cooler . All information listed in this position announcement will be used by Human Resources, the Hiring Department, and Civil Rights & Title IX for screening, interviewing and selection purposes. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at UND.humanresources@UND.edu or contact us by phone at 701-777-4226. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Veteran’s Preference Veterans claiming preference must submit all proof of eligibility by the closing date. Proof of eligibility includes a DD-214 or a copy of NGB 22 from National Guard or Reserve (with a unit located in ND) or certification from the applicant's unit command that the individual is expected to be discharged or released from active duty in the uniformed services under other than dishonorable conditions not later than one hundred twenty days after the date of the submission of the certification. If claiming disabled veteran status, proof of eligibility includes a DD-214 and a current letter of disability dated within the past year. Confidentiality of Application Materials Pursuant to NDCC 44-04-18.27, applications and any records related to the applications that identify an applicant are confidential, except records related to the finalists of the position, which are open to the public after the search committee has identified the top three or more finalists who will be invited to campus. EEO Statement The University of North Dakota is an equal opportunity employer (veteran/disability). All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin (including shared ancestry/ethnicity), religion, sex, age, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran's status, or other protected characteristic. Veterans and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Campus Crime Statistics Act, the University of North Dakota publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at UND.edu. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the UND Police Department located at 3851 Campus Road, Grand Forks, ND, 58202. Before you go! Want to be notified of jobs as we post them? First Name (required) 5a6e0360 Last Name (required) 9081467c Email (required) 50d429ac Job Alert afdbe3f8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Teaching & Leadership Teaching & Leadership Categories Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you for your interest in applying to the University of North Dakota Close Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
