    "https://careers.und.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-management-tenure-track-grand-forks-north-dakota-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Management, Tenure Track - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Assistant Professor of Management, Tenure Track - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Management, Tenure Track Apply Now Assistant Professor of Management, Tenure Track 499427 Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Full-time Faculty Salary/Position Classification $140,000+ Dependent on Experience, 9-month contract 40 hours per week This position will work onsite at UND Grand Forks, ND campus Purpose of Position The Middleton School of Entrepreneurship & Management at the University of North Dakota seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Management. The successful candidate will teach up to five courses a year in our supply chain management program including introductory and advanced courses both in person and online. The position also includes mentoring students and developing and maintaining a research agenda aligned with AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) standards. The successful candidate will be expected to publish research related to the discipline. Service to the department, college, university, and profession will also be an important part of the position. Established in 1883, the University of North Dakota is the oldest research university in North Dakota. Founded with a strong liberal arts foundation, it is the state’s flagship university and is classified by the Carnegie Foundation as having very high research activity. UND offers degrees in more than 225 fields of study with nearly 16,000 students. It is the home of the state’s only School of Law and School of Medicine. The School of Medicine and Health Sciences has major initiatives in rural and public health, and Aerospace is home to one of the first and largest unmanned aerial vehicle programs in the world. UND is located in Grand Forks, North Dakota, a vibrant college town of roughly 60,000 people located on the border of North Dakota and Minnesota. Short commutes, a great public-school system, high quality medical facilities, low crime, ample parks and theaters, and a cost of living below that found in large American cities are some of Grand Forks’ advantages. Ranked as one of the top 5 Best Small College Towns, and America’s Best Hockey Town, Grand Forks offers stellar quality of life without the metropolitan hassles. Duties & Responsibilities Teaching - demonstrate interest and ability to successfully develop rigorous courses that inspire students and prepare graduates for success in professional careers. Teaching assignments are expected to include courses in supply chain management but may include courses in other areas of management. Current technology, and high-impact teaching practices are incorporated across the curriculum. Research - demonstrate the ability to establish a productive research agenda. Service - faculty are expected to contribute to service within the department, college, university, and community. The Middleton School emphasizes professional involvement, and activities that enrich student experiences and career opportunities. Required Competencies The ability to teach, inspire, and mentor students Ability to work with and engage students and colleagues with a broad range of backgrounds within and outside of the Middleton School Effective interpersonal skills, including the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, and students Competence in using technology and ability to adopt new tools for both on-campus and online course delivery. Minimum Requirements An earned doctorate in Operations Management, Supply Chain Management, or closely related field from an AACSB accredited program/institution (ABD will be considered provided degree will be conferred prior to start date). Evidence of quality teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses Evidence of scholarly research activity commensurate with experience Evidence in support of AACSB Faculty Qualification standards for Scholarly Academic (SA) Successful completion of a Criminal History Background Check In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the US and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. This position does not support visa sponsorship for continued employment. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience in operations management, supply chain management, or a similar field. Demonstrated high-quality teaching effectiveness including high-impact practices and experiential learning. Experience advising/coaching/leading professionals or student groups To Apply To assure full consideration, applications must be received by November 16, 2026 , and include the following materials: Cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in position Curriculum vitae Documentation of quality teaching and scholarly research activity (job market paper). Applicants must provide documentation or evidence in support of their teaching accomplishments which may include teaching evaluations (including student evaluations), professional, supervisory, and, or peer evaluations, samples of teaching materials, etc. List of at least three references (including contact information) Unofficial transcripts. Please note that the selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts upon hire. Please note, all employment postings close at 11:55pm CST. Position Benefits Benefits include single or family health care coverage (UND pays the full premium), life insurance, employee assistance program, retirement plans with generous employer contributions, sick leave in addition to paid holidays. Optional benefits include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, supplemental retirement plans. UND also offers an employee tuition waiver and a variety of professional development opportunities . Find out more about UND's great benefits and perks ! Want to be notified of similar 