    "https://careers.und.edu/jobs/research-assistant-professor-grand-forks-north-dakota-united-states": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Research Assistant Professor - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Research Assistant Professor - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Kiosk mode Research Assistant Professor Apply Now Research Assistant Professor 499517 Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Full-time Faculty Salary/Position Classification $65,000-$75,000 annual, Exempt 40 hours per week This position will work onsite the Grand Forks, ND campus. Purpose of Position This position will require the Research Assistant Professor to work under the leadership of Dr. Colin Combs in the Department of Biomedical Sciences and manage a project related to understanding the reciprocal relationship between cancer and Alzheimer’s disease using a transgenic mouse model of Alzheimer’s disease and chemically induced colorectal cancer to study sex differences in both Alzheimer’s disease and cancer. The study will require mechanistic dissection of the relationships between the two diseases and any sex differences using histologic, molecular, and biochemical approach. Duties & Responsibilities Manage a research project related to interactions between cancer and Alzheimer’s disease using mouse models. Design and execute experimental approaches to test hypotheses related to colorectal cancer and Alzheimer’s disease. Interpret research outcomes and prepare/publish manuscripts related to colorectal cancer and Alzheimer's disease. Prepare and submit principal investigator extramural grant submissions. Participate in data collection and grant writing for additional laboratory proposals. Participate in additional collaborative research projects within the laboratory. Supervise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students. Participate in laboratory meetings through discussion and presentation. Present research findings and local and national conferences. Minimum Requirements Ph.D. in biomedical sciences or a related field. Experience working with mouse models of Alzheimer's disease Experience working with mouse models of colorectal cancer Experience in bioinformatics analysis Experience in histologic and biochemical analysis of the brain and colon Experience studying sex differences in cancer and Alzheimer’s disease Successful completion of a Criminal History Background Check In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the US and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Preferred Qualifications 5 years research experience after the award of a Ph.D Published proteomic and RNA seq analysis expertise Published experience studying the interactions between colon cancer and Alzheimer’s disease in mouse models Published experience studying sex differences in AD and cancer Published experience with human and mouse studies Extramural grant submission history and success To Apply To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by 10/21/2026 and include the following materials: Cover letter detailing suitability for the position and career goals A current curriculum vitae Please note, all employment postings close at 11:55pm CST. Position Benefits Benefits include single or family health care coverage (UND pays the full premium), life insurance, employee assistance program, retirement plans with generous employer contributions, sick leave in addition to paid holidays. Optional benefits include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, supplemental retirement plans. UND also offers an employee tuition waiver and a variety of professional development opportunities . Find out more about UND's great benefits and perks ! Want to be notified of similar opportunities? First Name (required) fd933ecd Last Name (required) ed719038 Email (required) 3dd9e44e Job Alert 9f579cb1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Biomedical Sciences Biomedical Sciences Categories Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you for your interest in applying to the University of North Dakota Categories: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Department: Biomedical Sciences Other UND Career Openings Post Doctoral Research Fellow Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Geriatrics Searching for a Postdoctoral fellow for the University of North Dakota, School of Medicine and Health Sciences, in the Geriatrics Department Laboratory. The primary focus of the laboratory is to determine the key regulators of stress and resiliency in humans, focused on the T cell stress response. Assistant Professor, Department of Mathematics & Statistics, Tenure Track Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Mathematics The Department of Mathematics & Statistics at the University of North Dakota is seeking an Assistant Professor of Statistics with a doctoral degree in statistics or a closely related area. This is a 9-month, tenure-track position, and the successful candidate will contribute to the department’s undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as contribute to the department’s scholarly and service missions. Department of Biomedical Sciences Chair and Professor, Tenured Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Biomedical Sciences The Chair of the Department of Biomedical Sciences will provide leadership and strategic direction for the department. This role involves overseeing and advancing the department's academic, research, and administrative functions, ensuring the highest standards of excellence in education, research, and service. Apply Now First Name (required) 25d39f7a Last Name (required) 4332239c Email (required) 68945682 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you Additional Information Find out why Grand Forks is Cooler . All information listed in this position announcement will be used by Human Resources, the Hiring Department, and Civil Rights & Title IX for screening, interviewing and selection purposes. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at UND.humanresources@UND.edu or contact us by phone at 701-777-4226. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Veteran’s Preference Veterans claiming preference must submit all proof of eligibility by the closing date. Proof of eligibility includes a DD-214 or a copy of NGB 22 from National Guard or Reserve (with a unit located in ND) or certification from the applicant's unit command that the individual is expected to be discharged or released from active duty in the uniformed services under other than dishonorable conditions not later than one hundred twenty days after the date of the submission of the certification. If claiming disabled veteran status, proof of eligibility includes a DD-214 and a current letter of disability dated within the past year. Confidentiality of Application Materials Pursuant to NDCC 44-04-18.27, applications and any records related to the applications that identify an applicant are confidential, except records related to the finalists of the position, which are open to the public after the search committee has identified the top three or more finalists who will be invited to campus. EEO Statement The University of North Dakota is an equal opportunity employer (veteran/disability). All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin (including shared ancestry/ethnicity), religion, sex, age, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran's status, or other protected characteristic. Veterans and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Campus Crime Statistics Act, the University of North Dakota publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at UND.edu. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the UND Police Department located at 3851 Campus Road, Grand Forks, ND, 58202. Before you go! Want to be notified of jobs as we post them? First Name (required) 1d63205e Last Name (required) b0dd8add Email (required) db84b5b0 Job Alert 7131f7e6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Biomedical Sciences Biomedical Sciences Categories Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you for your interest in applying to the University of North Dakota Close Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
