    "https://careers.und.edu/jobs/associate-dean-for-research-and-innovation-grand-forks-north-dakota-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Research and Innovation",
      "description": "Associate Dean for Research and Innovation - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Associate Dean for Research and Innovation - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Kiosk mode Associate Dean for Research and Innovation Apply Now Associate Dean for Research and Innovation 499444 Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Full-time Faculty Salary/Position Classification $95,000+ commensurate with discipline and experience for 9-month contract, plus additional administrative stipend of $7,500 and summer salary, Exempt 40 hours per week This position will work onsite at UND Grand Forks, ND campus Purpose of Position The College of Education & Human Development (CEHD) invites applications for a tenured faculty member at the rank of Professor to serve as Associate Dean for Research and Innovation, beginning July 1, 2027. Reporting directly to the Dean and serving as a member of CEHD's leadership team, the Associate Dean provides strategic and operational leadership for CEHD's research, scholarship, innovation, external funding, research administration and infrastructure, centers and institutes, and research impact. The Associate Dean will play a central role in advancing CEHD's research enterprise within the context of the University of North Dakota's R1 research mission. Working across departments, disciplines, centers, and external partnerships, the Associate Dean will help create the conditions for ambitious ideas to develop into sustained programs of research, scholarship, innovation, and impact. This position requires a leader who can recognize opportunities across traditional academic boundaries, connect people and resources, and strengthen the systems that support research. CEHD faculty, staff, and students engage in a broad range of disciplinary, interdisciplinary, methodological, and community-engaged scholarship across education, human development, behavioral and mental health, movement and health sciences, learning and technology, and related fields. The Associate Dean will support this breadth while helping faculty and research teams pursue increasingly significant external funding, collaboration, visibility, and scholarly impact. Duties & Responsibilities Lead development and implementation of a College-wide research and innovation strategy in partnership with the Dean, faculty, academic leaders, research staff, centers, and University partners. Identify and advance areas of research strength and emerging opportunity where CEHD has potential for distinctive regional, national, or international impact. Strengthen CEHD’s capacity to secure external funding, including large-scale, interdisciplinary, multi-investigator, training, center-level, and institutional awards. Foster interdisciplinary research teams and connect faculty with collaborators, funding opportunities, research infrastructure, and institutional resources. Provide strategic leadership and oversight for College-level sponsored research support, research administration, research investments, and use of research-related resources. Provide strategic coordination and oversight of CEHD centers, institutes, laboratories, and research initiatives, supporting their growth, sustainability, collaboration, and alignment with College priorities. Identify research infrastructure, staffing, technology, space, and other investments needed to strengthen CEHD’s research capacity and advise the Dean regarding strategic allocation of resources. Advance the translation and application of CEHD research and scholarship through partnerships with schools, healthcare organizations, communities, government, industry, tribal nations and communities, foundations, and other external partners. Foster a collaborative research culture that supports faculty research development, interdisciplinary scholarship, student engagement in research, and recognition and visibility of research accomplishments. Build relationships with funding agencies, foundations, research organizations, governmental entities, advancement partners, and other organizations that can strengthen CEHD’s research enterprise. Serve as a member of the Dean’s leadership team and advise the Dean on research strategy, sponsored programs, external funding, centers and institutes, innovation, infrastructure, and scholarly impact. Represent CEHD in University, regional, and national research initiatives, partnerships, committees, and leadership networks. - Required Competencies Demonstrated ability to build productive collaborations across disciplines, units, institutions, or organizations. Strong strategic, communication, organizational, and relationship-building skills. Demonstrated commitment to supporting excellence across diverse forms of research, scholarship, and methodology. Minimum Requirements Earned terminal degree in a field related to the disciplines within CEHD. Record of research, scholarship, and/or creative activity sufficient for appointment with tenure at the rank of Professor within an academic unit of CEHD. Demonstrated experience with externally funded research, sponsored projects, or significant grant development. Evidence of successful academic, research, or administrative leadership. Successful completion of criminal history background check In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the US and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. This position does not support visa sponsorship for continued employment. Preferred Qualifications Significant record of externally funded research or leadership of externally funded projects. Experience leading interdisciplinary or multi-investigator research teams and developing complex collaborative proposals. Experience providing leadership or oversight for research centers, institutes, laboratories, or similar initiatives. Experience with research administration, sponsored programs, grant personnel, or research-support infrastructure. Experience strategically managing research resources, budgets, F&A, space, or related infrastructure. Experience developing external partnerships that advance research, innovation, translation, or impact. Experience mentoring researchers and developing externally funded research programs. Experience working within a high-research-activity or R1 university environment. To Apply To assure full consideration, applications must be received by 10/26/2026 and include the following materials: Letter of interest Curriculum Vitae Contact information for 3 references or letters of reference Unofficial transcripts. Please note that the selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts upon hire. Please note, all employment postings close at 11:55pm CST. Position Benefits Benefits include single or family health care coverage (UND pays the full premium), life insurance, employee assistance program, retirement plans with generous employer contributions, sick leave in addition to paid holidays. Optional benefits include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, supplemental retirement plans. UND also offers an employee tuition waiver and a variety of professional development opportunities . Find out more about UND's great benefits and perks ! Want to be notified of similar opportunities? First Name (required) d1f26f9e Last Name (required) f8a1ff8d Email (required) b1565739 Job Alert 52422580 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Education & Human Development Education & Human Development Categories Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you for your interest in applying to the University of North Dakota Categories: Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Department: Education & Human Development Other UND Career Openings Associate Vice President for Research and Innovation/Chief Operating Officer Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States VP Research & Economic Dev The University of North Dakota is seeking candidates for the position of Associate Vice President for Research and Innovation / Chief Operating Officer (AVPRI/COO). UND is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission (HLC) and is classified Carnegie R1 (Very High Research Activity) with annual research expenditures approaching $200 million. Assistant Professor, Department of Mathematics & Statistics, Tenure Track Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Mathematics The Department of Mathematics & Statistics at the University of North Dakota is seeking an Assistant Professor of Statistics with a doctoral degree in statistics or a closely related area. This is a 9-month, tenure-track position, and the successful candidate will contribute to the department’s undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as contribute to the department’s scholarly and service missions. Senior Administrative Assistant for Training & Development Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Office of Human Resources The UND Office of Human Resources is seeking a Senior Administrative Assistant for Training & Development to support the Staff Career and Professional Development program. Join our team to directly support the professional growth of an entire campus community. Apply Now First Name (required) 092a8b9a Last Name (required) 50edc6be Email (required) 076df67f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you Additional Information Find out why Grand Forks is Cooler . All information listed in this position announcement will be used by Human Resources, the Hiring Department, and Civil Rights & Title IX for screening, interviewing and selection purposes. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at UND.humanresources@UND.edu or contact us by phone at 701-777-4226. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Veteran’s Preference Veterans claiming preference must submit all proof of eligibility by the closing date. Proof of eligibility includes a DD-214 or a copy of NGB 22 from National Guard or Reserve (with a unit located in ND) or certification from the applicant's unit command that the individual is expected to be discharged or released from active duty in the uniformed services under other than dishonorable conditions not later than one hundred twenty days after the date of the submission of the certification. If claiming disabled veteran status, proof of eligibility includes a DD-214 and a current letter of disability dated within the past year. Confidentiality of Application Materials Pursuant to NDCC 44-04-18.27, applications and any records related to the applications that identify an applicant are confidential, except records related to the finalists of the position, which are open to the public after the search committee has identified the top three or more finalists who will be invited to campus. EEO Statement The University of North Dakota is an equal opportunity employer (veteran/disability). All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin (including shared ancestry/ethnicity), religion, sex, age, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran's status, or other protected characteristic. Veterans and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Campus Crime Statistics Act, the University of North Dakota publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at UND.edu. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the UND Police Department located at 3851 Campus Road, Grand Forks, ND, 58202. Before you go! Want to be notified of jobs as we post them? First Name (required) 24dc6455 Last Name (required) 68015cae Email (required) 0d37b60f Job Alert f5201235 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Education & Human Development Education & Human Development Categories Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... 