    "https://careers.und.edu/jobs/open-rank-faculty-tenure-track-tenured-psychology-grand-forks-north-dakota-united-states": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty, Tenure-Track/Tenured, Psychology",
      "description": "Open Rank Faculty, Tenure-Track/Tenured, Psychology - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Open Rank Faculty, Tenure-Track/Tenured, Psychology - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Kiosk mode Open Rank Faculty, Tenure-Track/Tenured, Psychology Apply Now Open Rank Faculty, Tenure-Track/Tenured, Psychology 499506 Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Full-time Faculty Salary/Position Classification $75,000+, commensurate with rank, 9-month contract, Exempt 40 hours per week This position will work onsite at UND Gran Forks, ND campus Purpose of Position The Department of Psychology at the University of North Dakota (UND) seeks to fill a tenure-track/tenured faculty line at the Assistant/Associate/Full Professor rank and Director of the Indians into Psychology Doctoral Education (INPSYDE) program to begin in the Fall of 2027, contingent upon availability of funding. Candidates should have expertise in any area of Clinical or Counseling Psychology, and experience in Indigenous Mental Health. We seek candidates who demonstrate potential to secure external funding (Assistant level) or have demonstrated success in securing external funding (Associate and Full levels) and have experience working collaboratively with interdisciplinary partners, specifically with Indigenous populations. We seek an individual uniquely qualified to provide valuable cultural guidance and leadership to UND efforts to enhance and expand its research partnerships with area tribes, as well as all Indigenous research within the university. The Department of Psychology is an academic unit within the College of Arts & Sciences at UND. It serves approximately 18 full-time faculty members, 460 undergraduate majors, 300 minors, and 185 graduate students, with programs in Clinical (APA-accredited), Experimental, and Forensic Psychology. A Ph.D. in Clinical or Counseling Psychology from an APA-accredited program (completed by August 15, 2027), strong evidence of scholarly productivity and potential for establishing a funded research program, and evidence of teaching effectiveness are required. Demonstrated ability and willingness to work with groups with a broad range of backgrounds is preferred. Promotion in this position will be tied to success in establishing and maintaining a strong, externally fundable research program and excelling in teaching. UND is supportive of dual-career assistance both within the University and the local community. Please contact UND’s Recruiting Manager, Hannah Whalen (Hannah.Whalen@UND.edu), to explore dual-career opportunities. Duties & Responsibilities Direct the Indians into Psychology Doctoral Education (INPSYDE) Program, including managing the INPSYDE Program and Grant. Produce peer-reviewed publications within the area of research expertise and seek external grant funding. Teach a mix of online and on-campus courses in both the undergraduate and graduate programs and supervise graduate students, including clinical supervision of graduate students working in our training clinic. All faculty are expected to contribute service to the department, college, university, and community. UND and the College of Arts & Sciences seek applicants who are committed to helping students from underrepresented backgrounds succeed. The successful candidate’s contract effort will include teaching, research, service, and administrative responsibilities. The position includes a course reduction during the first year, with the teaching load thereafter adjusted based on continued funding from Indian Health Service (IHS). Continued IHS funding may also provide opportunities for summer support. The successful candidate will demonstrate outstanding potential to establish and sustain a research program that attracts external funding and aligns with the UND LEADS Strategic Plan. Required Competencies Ability to teach a mix of online and on-campus courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Effective interpersonal skills, including the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, and students. Ability and willingness to work with groups with a broad range of backgrounds. Ability and willingness to supervise graduate students (including clinical supervision of our graduate students in our training clinic) and contribute to service within the department, college, university, and/or community. Ability to produce peer-reviewed publications within the area of research expertise and seek external grant funding. Minimum Requirements Earned Ph.D. in Clinical or Counseling Psychology by August 15, 2027. Licensed/License Eligible in North Dakota. Published scholarly work. Served as instructor of record or teaching assistant for an undergraduate or graduate course. Experience within and/or across Native communities. Successful completion of a Criminal History Background Check In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the US and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Preferred Qualifications Strong evidence of scholarly productivity. Experience in research in Indigenous Mental Health. Experience with administering an Indian Health Services Section 217 funding. Demonstrated success in seeking external funding. Experience working collaboratively with interdisciplinary partners, with preference for intertribal and intratribal entities. To Apply To assure full consideration, applications must be received by 11/16/2026 and include the following materials: Cover letter CV Contact information for a minimum of three references Unofficial transcripts. Please note that the selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts upon hire. Further information may be requested later (e.g., letters of recommendation, a graduate transcript, teaching evaluations). The position is open until filled. Questions can be directed to Dr. Andre Kehn, Chair, Department of Psychology: andre.kehn@und.edu Please note, all employment postings close at 11:55pm CST. Position Benefits Benefits include single or family health care coverage (UND pays the full premium), life insurance, employee assistance program, retirement plans with generous employer contributions, sick leave in addition to paid holidays. Optional benefits include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, supplemental retirement plans. UND also offers an employee tuition waiver and a variety of professional development opportunities . Find out more about UND's great benefits and perks ! Want to be notified of similar opportunities? First Name (required) ad8bdf18 Last Name (required) 5a1d4918 Email (required) 89d125ca Job Alert 7063b11f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Psychology Psychology Categories Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you for your interest in applying to the University of North Dakota Categories: Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Department: Psychology Other UND Career Openings Associate Dean for Research and Innovation Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Education & Human Development The College of Education & Human Development invites applications to lead our college as the Associate Dean for Research and Innovation. Research Assistant Professor Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Biomedical Sciences Manage a project related to understanding the reciprocal relationship between cancer and Alzheimer’s disease using a transgenic mouse model of Alzheimer’s disease and chemically induced colorectal cancer to study sex differences in both Alzheimer’s disease and cancer. Part-time Instructional Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Dean's Office A&S The College of Arts & Sciences seeks a part-time instructor to teach A&S 351: Intro to Law & Legal Studies. This is an on-campus course. Apply Now First Name (required) 16987278 Last Name (required) 04b20b41 Email (required) ac6839d7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you Additional Information Find out why Grand Forks is Cooler . All information listed in this position announcement will be used by Human Resources, the Hiring Department, and Civil Rights & Title IX for screening, interviewing and selection purposes. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at UND.humanresources@UND.edu or contact us by phone at 701-777-4226. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Veteran’s Preference Veterans claiming preference must submit all proof of eligibility by the closing date. Proof of eligibility includes a DD-214 or a copy of NGB 22 from National Guard or Reserve (with a unit located in ND) or certification from the applicant's unit command that the individual is expected to be discharged or released from active duty in the uniformed services under other than dishonorable conditions not later than one hundred twenty days after the date of the submission of the certification. If claiming disabled veteran status, proof of eligibility includes a DD-214 and a current letter of disability dated within the past year. Confidentiality of Application Materials Pursuant to NDCC 44-04-18.27, applications and any records related to the applications that identify an applicant are confidential, except records related to the finalists of the position, which are open to the public after the search committee has identified the top three or more finalists who will be invited to campus. EEO Statement The University of North Dakota is an equal opportunity employer (veteran/disability). All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin (including shared ancestry/ethnicity), religion, sex, age, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran's status, or other protected characteristic. Veterans and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Campus Crime Statistics Act, the University of North Dakota publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at UND.edu. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the UND Police Department located at 3851 Campus Road, Grand Forks, ND, 58202. Before you go! Want to be notified of jobs as we post them? First Name (required) c44b88f7 Last Name (required) 3bf5e8aa Email (required) d41bbafa Job Alert 9d669ee7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Psychology Psychology Categories Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you for your interest in applying to the University of North Dakota Close Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
