    "https://careers.und.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-accountancy-tenure-track-grand-forks-north-dakota-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accountancy, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Accountancy, Tenure Track - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Assistant Professor of Accountancy, Tenure Track - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Accountancy, Tenure Track Apply Now Assistant Professor of Accountancy, Tenure Track 499398 Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Full-time Faculty Salary/Position Classification $150,000 9-month contract, Exempt 40 hours per week This position will work onsite at UND Grand Forks, ND Purpose of Position The successful candidate will teach up to five courses a year in our accountancy program including introductory and advanced courses both in person and online. The position also includes mentoring students and developing and maintaining a research agenda aligned with AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) standards. The successful candidate will be expected to publish research related to the discipline. Service to the department, college, university, and profession will also be an important part of the position. Duties & Responsibilities Teaching - demonstrate interest and ability to successfully develop rigorous courses that inspire students and prepare graduates for success in professional careers. Teaching assignments are expected to include courses in financial accounting but may include courses in other areas of accounting. Data analytics, current technology, and high-impact teaching practices are incorporated across the accounting curriculum. Research - demonstrate the ability to establish a productive research agenda. Service - faculty are expected to contribute to service within the department, college, university, and community. The Herr School of Accountancy emphasizes alumni engagement, professional involvement, and activities that enrich student experiences and career opportunities. Required Competencies The ability to teach, inspire, and mentor students Ability to work with and engage diverse students and colleagues within and outside of the Herr school of Accountancy Effective interpersonal skills, including the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, and students Competence in using technology and ability to adopt new tools for both on-campus and online course delivery. Minimum Requirements Ph.D. in Accounting or Business with an accounting emphasis/concentration/major from an AACSB accredited program (ABD will be considered provided degree will be conferred prior start date). Evidence of quality teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses Evidence of scholarly research activity commensurate with experience Evidence in support of AACSB Faculty Qualification standards for Scholarly Academic (SA) Successful completion of a Criminal History Background Check In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the US and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. This position does not support visa sponsorship for continued employment. Preferred Qualifications Professional accounting experience Professional accounting certification To Apply To assure full consideration, applications must be received by November 1, 2026 , and include the following materials: Cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in position Curriculum vitae Documentation of quality teaching and scholarly research activity (job market paper) List of at least three references (including contact information) Unofficial transcripts. Please note that the selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts upon hire. Position open until filled Please note, all employment postings close at 11:55pm CST. Position Benefits Benefits include single or family health care coverage (UND pays the full premium), life insurance, employee assistance program, retirement plans with generous employer contributions, sick leave in addition to paid holidays. Optional benefits include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, supplemental retirement plans. UND also offers an employee tuition waiver and a variety of professional development opportunities . Find out more about UND's great benefits and perks ! Want to be notified of similar opportunities? First Name (required) 4046cffe Last Name (required) 69716229 Email (required) 0eac76e3 Job Alert 9fe60e06 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Accountancy Accountancy Categories Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you for your interest in applying to the University of North Dakota Categories: Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Department: Accountancy Other UND Career Openings There are currently no jobs matching this criteria Apply Now First Name (required) e84cc0f6 Last Name (required) 6a5fc068 Email (required) 8a8cbe8b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you A