    "https://careers.und.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-forensic-science-tenure-track-grand-forks-north-dakota-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Forensic Science, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Forensic Science, Tenure Track - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Assistant Professor of Forensic Science, Tenure Track - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Forensic Science, Tenure Track Apply Now Assistant Professor of Forensic Science, Tenure Track 498876 Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Full-time Faculty Salary/Position Classification $76,000+, Dependent on Experience, 9-month contract, Exempt 40 hours per week This position will work onsite at UND Grand Forks, ND campus Purpose of Position The Forensic Science Program in the College of Arts & Sciences at the University of North Dakota invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Forensic Science. We seek candidates with an active, forensic science-focused research agenda, demonstrated by publications in peer-reviewed journals, presentations at professional conferences (e.g., AAFS), and the pursuit of external funding through submissions to state, federal, and other funding agencies. The successful candidate will be expected to have a 2/2 teaching load in the B.S. and M.S. Forensic Science programs, mentor undergraduate and graduate students, and submit at least one federal grant proposal within the first two years of employment. By Year 3, the teaching load will increase to a 2/3 depending on the level of external grant support. The successful hire will be expected to establish and sustain an externally funded research program focused primarily on forensic biology, contributing to the continued growth and national prominence of the Forensic Science Program. Established in 1883, the University of North Dakota is the oldest research university in North Dakota. Founded with a strong liberal arts foundation, it is the state’s flagship university and is classified by the Carnegie Foundation as having very high research activity. UND offers degrees in more than 225 fields of study and enrolls nearly 16,000 students. It is the home of the state’s only School of Law and School of Medicine. The School of Medicine and Health Sciences has major initiatives in rural and public health, and Aerospace is home to one of the first and largest unmanned aerial vehicle programs in the world. UND is located in Grand Forks, North Dakota, a vibrant college town of over 57,000 people located on the border of North Dakota and Minnesota. Short commutes, a great public-school system, high quality medical facilities, low crime, ample parks and theaters, and a cost of living below that found in large American cities are some of Grand Forks’ advantages. Ranked as one of the top 5 Best Small College Towns, and America’s Best Hockey Town, Grand Forks offers stellar quality of life without the metropolitan hassles. Duties & Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the B.S. and M.S. Forensic Science programs (typically a 2/2 or 2/3 teaching load) and mentor undergraduate and graduate students. Develop and maintain an active research program in forensic biology, including the publication of scholarly work and involvement of students in research activities. Pursue external funding to support research initiatives, including submission of at least one federal grant proposal within the first two years of employment. Maintain active engagement with the forensic science profession through scholarly presentations, professional service, and participation in organizations such as AAFS and ASCLD; promote the highest standards of scientific integrity, ethical practice, and professional conduct; and contribute to program, college, and university service. Required Competencies Excellent written and oral communication skills, including the ability to teach, inspire, and mentor undergraduate and graduate students. Demonstrated commitment to scientific integrity, ethical practice, professionalism, and responsible conduct in research, teaching, service, and student mentorship. Strong interpersonal and collaborative skills, with the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, and staff. Excellent organizational, time-management, and research management skills, including the ability to meet deadlines, and provide timely, professional, and constructive communication and feedback to students, colleagues, and program stakeholders. Proficiency with computer technologies and software applications relevant to teaching, research, and professional activities. Minimum Requirements Ph.D. in Forensic Science or a closely related field with a focus on Forensic Biology, completed by August 15, 2027. Successful completion of a Criminal History Background Check In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the US and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated expertise and experience in forensic biology, including research, applied forensic science practice, and/or experience in a forensic science laboratory. Evidence of teaching effectiveness at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Record of peer-reviewed publications demonstrating scholarly contributions to forensic biology / forensic science. Evidence of an active research agenda with the potential to establish and sustain an externally funded research program, demonstrated through successful acquisition of external funding and/or strong potential to secure funding in support of scholarly research activities. Evidence of scholarly dissemination through presentations at regional, national, or international scientific conferences (e.g., American Academy of Forensic Sciences Annual Scientific Conference). Active membership and engagement in professional organizations relevant to forensic science (e.g., AAFS, ASCLD, or related professional societies). Research interests that align with UND's Rural Health & Communities Grand Challenge (https://und.edu/research/grand-challenges/). To Apply To assure full consideration, applications must be received by 11/02/2026 and include the following materials: Cover letter. Curriculum Vitae, including academic credentials, professional experience, peer-reviewed publications, scholarly presentations, extramural funding, and professional activities and memberships (e.g., American Academy of Forensic Sciences). Research statement describing current research activities, future research plans, and potential opportunities for student involvement. Teaching philosophy statement. Contact information for three professional references. Unofficial transcripts. Please note that the selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts upon hire. Position is open until filled. Questions can be directed to the Forensic Science Program Director, Lavinia Iancu at lavinia.iancu@und.edu. Please note, all employment postings close at 11:55pm CST. Position Benefits Benefits include single or family health care coverage (UND pays the full premium), life insurance, employee assistance program, retirement plans with generous employer contributions, sick leave in addition to paid holidays. Optional benefits include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, supplemental retirement plans. UND also offers an employee tuition waiver and a variety of professional development opportunities . Find out more about UND's great benefits and perks ! Want to be notified of similar opportunities? First Name (required) bc6e4341 Last Name (required) 7fff98a7 Email (required) dc6e8670 Job Alert 040158f2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Criminal Justice Criminal Justice Categories Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Employment Type