      "title": "Assistant Professor, Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Physical Therapy - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Assistant Professor, Physical Therapy - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Physical Therapy Apply Now Assistant Professor, Physical Therapy 498459 Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Full-time Faculty Salary/Position Classification $89,000+ annual, Exempt 40 hours per week This position will work onsite the Grand Forks, ND campus. Purpose of Position The Department of Physical Therapy is seeking a faculty member to teach in the areas of neurologic, geriatric, general physical therapy, and other duties dependent of departmental need. Duties & Responsibilities Teaching in the areas of neurologic, geriatric, general physical therapy, and other areas of departmental need. Well-defined, ongoing scholarly agenda and dissemination. Service to the department, school, university, and profession. Advising graduate and undergraduate students. Required Competencies Possess appropriate academic and experiential qualifications. Obtain and hold appropriate state licensure for professional practice. Maintain a high level of professional ethics as outlined by APTA and the University. Have strong interpersonal and written communication skills. Minimum Requirements Academic doctorate or earned DPT with a commitment to pursue academic doctorate appropriate for teaching responsibilities and scholarly activity. Advanced training with contemporary expertise and clinical experience in neurologic, geriatric, or generalist physical therapy practice. Current PT license; eligible for ND license. 3 years' clinical experience. Successful completion of a Criminal History Background Check. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the US and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. This position does not support visa sponsorship for continued employment. Preferred Qualifications An academic doctorate in a field appropriate for teaching responsibilities. A Board-Certified Clinical Specialist from the American Board of Physical Therapy Specialties or advanced certification. Classroom teaching experience. Experience in clinical research or scholarly activity. Membership and involvement in professional associations To Apply To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by 08/26/2026 and include the following materials: Letter of interest Current curriculum vitae Contact information for 3 professional references Position is opened until filled. Please note, all employment postings close at 11:55pm CST. Position Benefits Benefits include single or family health care coverage (UND pays the full premium), life insurance, employee assistance program, retirement plans with generous employer contributions, sick leave in addition to paid holidays. Optional benefits include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, supplemental retirement plans. UND also offers an employee tuition waiver and a variety of professional development opportunities . Find out more about UND's great benefits and perks ! Want to be notified of similar opportunities? First Name (required) 4f8f9dd1 Last Name (required) 1c5951d4 Email (required) 82dd7f2e Job Alert 4a31617e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Physical Therapy Physical Therapy Categories Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & da