    "https://careers.und.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-digital-journalism-media-production-tenure-track-grand-forks-north-dakota-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Digital Journalism & Media Production, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Digital Journalism & Media Production, Tenure Track - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Assistant Professor, Digital Journalism & Media Production, Tenure Track - Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Digital Journalism & Media Production, Tenure Track Apply Now Assistant Professor, Digital Journalism & Media Production, Tenure Track 498434 Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Full-time Faculty Salary/Position Classification $65,000 9-month contract, Exempt 40 hours per week This position will work onsite at UND Grand Forks, ND campus Purpose of Position The Department of Communication at the University of North Dakota seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Communication focusing on digital journalism and media production. We are seeking applicants who have expertise in multimedia journalism and production within diverse social, cultural, political, and global contexts and who employ a wide range of research methods to explore major issues in digital journalism. The successful candidate will be expected to conduct research, teach relevant journalism courses, and provide students with experiential learning opportunities in our new recording studios. The University of North Dakota is supportive of dual-career assistance both within the University and the local community. Please be sure to notify our Recruiting Manager, Hannah Whalen ( Hannah.Whalen@UND.edu ) right away to explore dual-career opportunities. Duties & Responsibilities The successful applicant will receive an initial contract with an approximate effort distribution of 50% teaching, 40% research, and 10% service. We value diverse perspectives and actively seek applicants committed to the success of our students. The successful candidate will have an annual teaching load of 2/2 and be expected to teach undergraduate-level journalism courses face-to-face and online. Course assignments may include but are not limited to, Introduction to Journalism, News Writing Fundamentals in the Online World, Audio Production and Broadcasting, Multimedia Reporting and Storytelling, and Senior Capstone in Communication. Graduate-level (M.A. and Ph.D.) teaching is also expected, with courses potentially including Professional Project in Communication and Qualitative Communication Research. Assigned courses will be consistent with the candidate’s area of expertise. Additionally, the new hire will be expected to contribute to the development and supervision of a student-run multimedia production studio facility in the future. Publishing peer-reviewed journal articles and applying for competitive external grants on a regular basis will be expected for tenure. Required Competencies Ability to conduct and publish scientific studies Excellent written and oral communication skills, including evidence of the ability to teach, inspire, and mentor students Effective interpersonal skills, including the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, and students Ability and willingness to work with and engage diverse students and colleagues within and outside the Department of Communication Ability to adapt to current methods of teaching and research, including online delivery and integration of artificial intelligence Minimum Requirements Ph.D. in Communication or related discipline by 8/15/2027 Successful completion of a Criminal History Background Check In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the US and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience in digital media production Evidence of track record of research, teaching, education, and/or professional experience related to journalism Experience being part of an externally (grant)-funded research team(s) Evidence of applying for and/or obtaining external funding Experience incorporating artificial intelligence (AI) into research and teaching Experience offering students experiential learning opportunities Experience teaching both undergraduate-level and graduate-level courses in a Department of Communication’s curriculum Experience teaching online courses To Apply To assure full consideration, applications must be received by 09/30/2026 and include the following materials: Letter of application Curriculum vitae List of at least three references (including contact information) Position is open until filled. Questions can be directed to the Department Chair, Joonghwa Lee, at joonghwa.lee@und.edu. Please note, all employment postings close at 11:55pm CST. Position Benefits Benefits include single or family health care coverage (UND pays the full premium), life insurance, employee assistance program, retirement plans with generous employer contributions, sick leave in addition to paid holidays. Optional benefits include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, supplemental retirement plans. UND also offers an employee tuition waiver and a variety of professional development opportunities . Find out more about UND's great benefits and perks ! Want to be notified of similar opportunities? First Name (required) 94a8aa27 Last Name (required) 3683df5b Email (required) d94a19d6 Job Alert 71a9eb93 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Communication Dept Communication Dept Categories Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Employment Type Full-time Faculty Full-time Faculty Locations Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at UND. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Terms of Use . Thank you for your interest in applying to the University of North Dakota Categories: Tenure/Tenure-track Faculty Department: Communication Dept Other UND Career Openings Assistant Professor, Communication, Tenure Track Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Communication Dept The Department of Communication at the University of North Dakota seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Communication with expertise in one or more of the following areas: international/intercultural communication, interpersonal communication, organizational communication, sports communication, strategic communication, and communication and technology. Assistant Professor, Strategic Communication, Tenure Track Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Communication Dept The Department of Communication at the University of North Dakota seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Communication focusing on strategic communication strategic communication, such as advertising and public relations, who employs quantitative, qualitative, and/or computational research methods. Assistant Professor, Health & Science Communication, Tenure Track Grand Forks, North Dakota, United States Communication Dept The Department of Communication at the University of North Dakota seeks a tenure-track assistant professor who has expertise in science and health communication within diverse social, cultural, political, and global contexts and who employs either qualitative, quantitative, and/or computational research methods. Apply Now First Name (required) 28658d1b Last Name (required) 6b966d0d Email (required) 9ca0f506 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working 